**Verdict:** trust **strained**, value **high**, delight **clear_hit** — recommendation **revise**, with **1 blocker** and 5 concerns.

**The blocker (SUBJECT-B1):** the coin-pitching anecdote is inverted against Jordan. The draft has him "hitting them with the famous shrug when he won" against his security guards; the documented Last Dance scene has guard John Michael Wozniak *beating Jordan* and shrugging *at him* — the packet's own sources (NBC Sports, Action Network) confirm the contradiction. The fix actually strengthens the thesis: he built stakes so real that losing $20 to his own guard was an event.

**Strongest hit:** the Hall of Fame reframe — "He was not taking a victory lap. He was disclosing his fuel source, in front of the fire marshals, while crying." My research found this matches Jordan's own post-speech defense to Ahmad Rashad ("If you understood it from my perspective then you would understand"), so the draft independently reached the reading Jordan publicly asked for. I flagged adding one sentence of that defense as an improvement.

**Highest-priority concern (SUBJECT-C1):** the freeze-out hedge is erased. On the Hall of Fame podium Jordan said "if it was a rumor I never took it as truth," but the grievance ledger cites the freeze-out without it — making him look credulous where the record shows him precise. Restoring the hedge is one clause and actually sharpens the draft's own "truth was never the input" thesis.

One packet question also resolved in the draft's favor: "Now he's got me" is verbatim per SI, CBS Sports, and Variety coverage of the Kobe memorial.
